# UI, PWA, and Accessibility

## Delivery model

- One responsive installable Progressive Web Application.
- Do not create Flutter, React Native, or native mobile apps in initial phases.
- Mobile-first for operators; tablet/desktop for QA, administration, and management.

## Stack

- Django Templates + HTMX + Tailwind CSS.
- Minimal JavaScript; Alpine.js only for small client-side state.
- IndexedDB may be used later for offline drafts and sync queues.

## Operator UX

- Minimize typing; prefer selection, scanning, and structured inputs.
- Normal operator workflow must aim to be faster than paper.
- Sinhala support is mandatory for operator-facing content; English for administrative/QA surfaces as confirmed by stakeholders.

## Accessibility

- Target WCAG-aligned practices for interactive controls, labels, contrast, and keyboard use.
- Error states must be visible and actionable.
- Do not rely on color alone to convey critical status.

## Design handoff

- UI work follows Figma Professional journeys and design-system handoff.
- Do not invent unchecked visual patterns that conflict with the approved design system once published.
